1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:08,645
Can, could, may, might, will, would, shall, should and must do not describe an action; they comment on it: how possible, how necessary, how polite.

2
00:00:08,645 --> 00:00:11,119
And they obey five rules.

3
00:00:11,119 --> 00:00:16,276
One: no s in the third person: he can swim, not he cans.

4
00:00:16,276 --> 00:00:20,872
Two: a bare infinitive, without to: she must go.

5
00:00:20,872 --> 00:00:22,226
Only ought keeps to.

6
00:00:22,226 --> 00:00:26,770
Three: no do in questions or negatives: can he drive?

7
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:32,057
Four: never two modals together: not will can, but will be able to.

8
00:00:32,057 --> 00:00:39,804
Five: no ing form and no participle; for those, use a semi modal like be able to.

